{
  "id": "age-structured-epidemic-who-epi",
  "name": "Age-Structured Epidemic Model",
  "description": "Illustrative Age-Structured Epidemic Model.\n\nSource reconciliation 2026-10-20: Illustrative two-age SIR system inspired by age-assortative contact concepts. Mossong et al. is an empirical contact-diary study; no extraction, aggregation or reciprocity adjustment supports the hard-coded contacts 15, 5 and 10, Beta 0.3, infectious duration 7 or the initial populations. The same cross-contact value is used in both directions despite different group sizes; empirical matrix fidelity is not established. The preceding source-only reconciliation preserved equations, initial values, flow topology and layout. Scientific/source fidelity remains unverified.\n\nVersion 1.8 changes only the numerical method to explicit Radau on the existing one-day output grid. The unchanged two-age SIR ODE preserves each age population and nonnegative compartments, but daily Euler steps violate the infection depletion timescale and create negative susceptibles. Independent reference/convergence and age-specific mass-balance checks validate numerical integration; the contact matrix, reciprocity and empirical calibration remain unverified.",
  "stocks": [
